 "evidence": "CM1's RRTMG longwave, compiled from the lunar build's objects into an offline driver, and the atmosphere domain's correlated-k model on the same clear-sky layers of the ring's cloud-free columns, as CM1 hands them to RRTMG, and of twins scaled inside RRTMG's tables, with CM1's stored lwten turned back into RRTMG's rate (cm1_output.py); means over the sampled columns. A diagnosis of one ring's columns over its second lunar day.",
 "reading_rule": "K/day of temperature at constant pressure, negative cools, mass-weighted over the GCM's lowest four layers, over the layers below the table's edge and over those above it to 13.74 km. rrtmg_minus_correlated_k on the columns against the twins gives the extrapolation's share of RRTMG's error; edge_held_minus_as_built how far the extrapolated layers depend on the extrapolation; cm1_minus_rrtmg CM1's call against the same RRTMG offline. cm1_as_written is the tendency CM1 stores, at constant volume, cp/cvm times RRTMG's rate under eqtset 2."
